# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-17; notes.md finding F-1). A variable bound over the root events reads any kind's legs and
# attributes by name at run, as on 2.0 (check3.movement_field: "a movement of a kind not known statically"), so a
# field read with no test loads, and a movement without it refuses the run (LOAD-FIELD at run, as 2.0 printed). L §5.7's
# "stays refused, as in 2.0 (LOAD-FIELD ...)" (2.1-F1): events keeps 2.0's reading (the lead lists it at G2).
# pay has no heir.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key persons
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input inh_day: date
input pay_day: date
input amt: money PLN
move inh: inheritances
  on inh_day
  attr heir = tomek
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
def share[m in events, p in parties]: num = if p == m.heir then 1 else 0 at m.day
ask q: share[inh, ania], share[inh, tomek], share[pay, ania], share[pay, tomek]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  inh_day = 2026-03-02
  pay_day = 2026-03-03
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
refused: LOAD-FIELD heir is not a field of pay
